hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1407","From Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam, from his origin, from Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, that he heard Abbad bin Tamim, saying: Abdullah bin Zaid said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to rain rain. So he delivered a sermon, faced the qiblah, supplicated, asked for water, changed his robe and prayed with them.”"
